.TH "GIT-SIS" "1" "2026-08-17" "pylitfun" "Git-Verbs Manual"
.SH NAME
git-sis, gsis \- list the untracked and ignored files, without deleting anything
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git sis
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git sis
lists the files and directories that
.BR git-cl (1)
would delete, without deleting anything, by running
.BR "git status --ignored --short" .
.PP
Unlike
.BR git-cl (1)
and
.BR git-rhu (1),
.B git sis
changes nothing, so it asks for no confirmation.
.SH QUIRKS
Before running
.BR "git status --ignored --short" ,
.B git sis
prints two reminder lines about what that command will not show you, without running either of
them:
.RS 4
find . \-type p
.br
find . \-type d \-empty \-not \-path '*/.git/*'
.RE
.PP
That is: untracked named pipes, and empty directories, neither of which
.B git status
lists.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits with the status of the
.B git status
it ran.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
git sis
.RS 4
List every untracked and ignored file and directory, plus the two reminder lines above.
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-status (1),
.BR git-clean (1),
.BR git-cl (1)
